    {
      "id": "claim_48b8dee5e010415090f9e52acf3be353",
      "statement": "An invitation links an email to a team with a target role, and the service emails two links (`/auth/activate` for a new user, `/invitations/accept` for an existing one) that both route to the same `Accept` component. Both `email` and `token` query params are required; missing either shows the invalid-link panel. `getInvitation(email, token)` runs on init and branches on `invitation().isNewUser` into three outcomes: activate with a password (new user), log in then `acceptInvite(token)` (existing user signed out), or one-click `acceptInvite(token)` (existing user signed in). Because the route has no guard, the component restores the session by hand via `checkSession()` whenever `getToken()` is truthy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L23-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90e8265aad5742d632cf7f685b5afa59ea90df42cc1ecd88d582193a28c5e565:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L63-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5531f44169d9f6a0742519fd314515a81f7d9a86fc2f61bd248a72bcca02b7c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ecd1451a0c384f6385c5614ec7dffea4",
      "statement": "If `getInvitation()` returns 404 and the user has a stored token, the accept page navigates to `/` instead of showing an invalid-link error — this handles a signed-in user revisiting an already-accepted invitation link after the consents gate reloads. A 404 with no session is a genuine invalid-or-expired link and is surfaced as an error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L50-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8901470c86d08a63b91082608f735def6e197d0ecf3471c323d44d2f680a6882:"
        }
