    {
      "id": "claim_67f1a4c260c046988c10f2d3a83a13b6",
      "statement": "`justSignedUp` is a module-level signal in `src/app/just-signed-up.ts`, true for exactly one page load after a fresh signup (email verification or OAuth) and never persisted. `consumeFragmentToken()` raises it from the `?flow=signup` query param and clears both that param and the `#access_token` fragment via `history.replaceState`; the Shell copies the flag into a local signal in its constructor and immediately resets the shared one to `false`, so the welcome banner is one-shot and cannot reappear on a later login. Because the flag is raised for OAuth signups too, the banner copy must not claim an email was verified.",
      "evidence": [
